{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"HANDOFF — epic 061c (LLM provider seam), continuing a /rebar-implement run.\n\n## WHERE TO WORK\nWorktree /Users/joeoakhart/rebar-wt-provider-seam on branch feat/llm-provider-seam.\nPrefix every command with the worktree venv: env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" <cmd>\nAn hourly cron loop (job ef01c04f, fires at :17) drives this epic; it is SESSION-ONLY and dies with the\nsession that created it, so a new session must re-create it if wanted.\n\n## GERRIT STACK — 10 deep, none submitted, they land together\n  1090  1903  temperature-deprecated family      gates pending\n  1086  343b  S5 provider provenance             gates pending\n  1081  3a98  pai preflight -> structured_run    +1/+1 GREEN\n  1067  281f  remove inert bedrock model id      Verified -1 (LOC-only)\n  1048  9249  S7 Bedrock IAM (ticket CLOSED)     Verified -1 (LOC-only)\n  1043  2932  S3 Bedrock provider (CLOSED)       Verified -1 (LOC-only)\n  1032  2682  runner split (CLOSED)              +1/+1\n  1023  dc0d  S4 OpenAI endpoint (CLOSED)        Verified -1 (LOC-only)\n  1014  f184  S2 capabilities (CLOSED)           Verified -1 (LOC-only)\n  1012  7468  S1 provider factory (CLOSED)       +1/+1\n\n## THE LOC SITUATION — READ BEFORE \"FIXING\" ANY RED VOTE\nThose -1s are ALL the module-size gate and NOTHING else. MEASURED runner.py per position:\n  7468=795  f184=802  dc0d=815  2682=670  2932=713  9249=713  281f=713  3a98=680  343b=689  1903=689\nMain's runner.py grew to 798 while this epic was in flight, so the chain now GROWS runner.py past the\n800 hard cap before it SPLITS it (2682), and 2932/9249/281f sit above 2682's own attested <700 test.\nReordering is IMPOSSIBLE: 2682's split captured dc0d's newer helper signature, and 3a98 moves code INTO\nthe module 2682 creates. A feature branch does NOT help (verified: submit requirements are inherited\nproject-wide, CI fires on feature-branch changes too — it is strictly MORE review).\nOPERATOR DECISION, already given: keep stacking; IGNORE any -1 that is ONLY the LOC gate; keep the TOP\nof the stack clean; the operator will MANUALLY OVERRIDE the red ancestors to submit. Do not re-litigate.\nGerrit submitted_together confirms all 10 form one submit set and 5 are submittable=False, so the\noverride is genuinely required — the top being green is not sufficient on its own.\n\n## BOARD\nCLOSED: 7468 S1, f184 S2, 2932 S3, dc0d S4, 9249 S7, 2682, 9f0b(bug), c083(bug, LANDED on main).\nIN PROGRESS (claimed, code committed, awaiting CI): 281f, 3a98, 343b S5, 1903.\nOPEN + BLOCKED: 0d76 S6 <- 3768 | eb6e S8 <- 3768,1903,a574 | 8625 S9 <- eb6e.\nOPEN + UNBLOCKED, do these next: a574 (region NoRegionError), 3768 (per-pass model seam).\nALSO FILED, not started: 7a79 (cache-warning floor), db1c (completion-recovery bound), c6c9 (attest.py\nat 800/800), 3a98 follow-ups. Epic 3147 + f161 (gate blindness) are separate.\n\n## WHAT WAS RUNNING WHEN THIS SESSION ENDED\n`rebar verify-completion <id> --ref HEAD` was mid-flight as a DRY RUN over 3a98, 281f, 1903, 343b — a\nread-only PASS/FAIL that does NOT close, used to find criterion defects BEFORE CI turns green. Re-run it;\nthree closes already failed this run on criterion defects, and each failure costs a full verifier run.\n\n## THE SINGLE MOST IMPORTANT RECURRING DEFECT: criteria the verifier cannot satisfy\nAn acceptance criterion whose evidence is EXTERNAL (a live call, a CI vote, container health, an AWS API\nresult) but which is left UNTAGGED is judged against the CODEBASE — a bar no repository can meet. S7 alone\nhad FIVE. A sweep found NINE more across six tickets, all now fixed. When writing any criterion, tag it\n[operator-attested] if its proof cannot live in the repo, and make sure the assertion is not vacuous.\nTwo real examples of vacuous ACs found and fixed: one required closing an already-closed ticket three more\ntimes; another asserted a BARE model id where `_model_id_of` returns None, so it would pass without ever\ntouching the table it existed to test.\n\n## PROCESS TRAPS THAT COST REAL TIME THIS RUN (all self-inflicted, all avoidable)\n1. zsh ate backticks as command substitution inside `rebar comment \"...\"`, silently STRIPPING symbol names\n   from a recorded ticket comment. Also `${VAR}:path` — a bare `$VAR:s...` applies zsh history modifiers\n   and mangled a git refspec. ALWAYS write ticket bodies via a heredoc file, and brace your variables.\n2. `make lint 2>&1 | tail -2 && ...` ALWAYS \"succeeds\" — a pipeline's exit status is tail's. This masked\n   lint failures, and the same shape in `git commit ... | tail && git push` pushed AFTER a FAILED commit.\n   Capture exit codes directly.\n3. A mutation check whose anchor does not match silently no-ops and looks identical to a test with teeth.\n   This happened THREE times (once the anchor hit a docstring, not the code). Always assert the mutation\n   applied, then assert the test went RED.\n4. Do NOT mutate the worktree while a gating suite runs in it — running a rebase during a background\n   pytest produced 8 spurious failures + 33 errors (\"Test moved the repo HEAD\"). conftest catches it.\n5. Commit gate: subject <=50, body <=72. Assert it programmatically; printing the length is not gating.\n\n## GATE MECHANICS\n- Use `--ref HEAD` / `REBAR_GATE_REF=HEAD` for EVERY gate; the default origin/main predates this stack.\n- The completion verifier reads COMMITTED state; uncommitted work reads as missing.\n- `rebar review-plan <id> --status` is a free currency check; a moving base ref silently staleness-invalidates.\n- `rebar sign-review <id>` re-signs from the recorded verdict with NO LLM re-run — use it when a review\n  PASSes but signing aborts.\n\n## AWS FACTS (project account 896586841071 / us-east-1 — CONFIRM before recording any measurement)\n- Only inference-profile ids work; plain on-demand ids ValidationException.\n- us./global. claude-opus-4-8 and opus-4-7 REJECT an explicit temperature (400). temp=1.0 succeeds, so it\n  is tunability that is deprecated. sonnet-4-6 accepts temperature. top_p is deprecated on opus-4-8 too\n  (latent: rebar never sets it). Fixed in 1903.\n- The review-bot container has NO aws CLI, NO AWS_* env vars and NO region: boto3 raises NoRegionError.\n  IMDS IS reachable (token 200, role resolves) but supplies NO region — the two are independent. See a574.\n- NEVER validate a scoped IAM grant from an admin/wildcard identity, and never stop at the policy\n  simulator: Converse authorizes against bedrock:InvokeModel, not bedrock:Converse. See infra/runbooks/\n  bedrock-access.md, now four sections including the boto3 streaming probe.\n\n## PERMISSIONS CHANGED THIS RUN\nContributors were granted create-only on refs/heads/feature/* (verified from the NON-admin identity;\ndelete deliberately withheld). Note the flow would ALSO need pushMerge on refs/for/refs/heads/main, which\nremains feature-branch-drivers only. The feature branch created for this epic was DELETED after it was\nproven not to help."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785461766482335001,"uuid":"1c78254a-3401-43f0-b46a-d1b81bf29afe"}